# React Component Guidelines

**React-specific development standards for consistent component architecture.**

## **Component Structure Requirements**

- **Use functional components only** - No class components
- **Use kebab-case filenames** for all React components

  ```
  // ✅ DO: Kebab-case files
  my-component.tsx
  user-profile.tsx

  // ❌ DON'T: Other naming conventions
  MyComponent.tsx
  userProfile.tsx
  ```

## **Import and Export Standards**

- **Don't import React** - Not needed in modern React/Next.js
- **Use PropsWithChildren** instead of manual children typing
- **Always use default export** for components
- **Use path aliases** from tsconfig.json e.g ~components for local packages and #ui for shared modules
- **Use `#ui` for UI components**

```tsx
// ✅ DO: Modern imports with path aliases and #ui for components
import { PropsWithChildren } from "react";
import { slugify } from "~utils/slugify";
import { Button } from "#ui/button";
import { Input } from "#ui/input";

// ❌ DON'T: Import React, relative paths unless necessary and ~modules/ui instead of #ui
import React, { PropsWithChildren } from "react";
import { slugify } from "../utils/slugify";
import { Button } from "~modules/ui/button";
```

## **Props and Component Structure**

- **Props interface must be named 'Props'** - Not ComponentProps or similar
- **Use destructuring in component parameters**
- **Preserve destructuring patterns** - Don't convert to object access

```tsx
// ✅ DO: Proper Props typing with destructuring
type Props = PropsWithChildren<{
  title: string;
  count: number;
}>;

const MyComponent = ({ children, title, count }: Props) => (
  <div>
    <h1>{title}</h1>
    <span>{count}</span>
    {children}
  </div>
);

// ❌ DON'T: Wrong Props name or object access
type MyComponentProps = { title: string };
const MyComponent = (props: MyComponentProps) => <div>{props.title}</div>;
```

## **Component Organization**

- **Move non-dependent code outside component** - Variables, constants, and functions that don't depend on props or hooks
- **Use immediate return** when possible
- **Add blank lines for logical grouping** - Between imports, variables, hooks, functions, and return statement

```tsx
// ✅ DO: Proper organization
import { useState } from "react";
import { slugify } from "~utils/slugify";

const STATIC_CONFIG = { maxItems: 10 };
const formatDate = (date: string) => new Date(date).toLocaleDateString();

type Props = {
  items: string[];
};

const MyComponent = ({ items }: Props) => {
  const [selected, setSelected] = useState<string>();

  const handleSelect = (item: string) => {
    setSelected(item);
  };

  return (
    <div>
      {items.map((item) => (
        <button key={item} onClick={() => handleSelect(item)}>
          {item}
        </button>
      ))}
    </div>
  );
};

export default MyComponent;
```

## **Refactoring Standards**

- **Preserve existing functionality** - Don't remove working features during refactoring
- **Maintain destructuring patterns** when refactoring components
- **Don't over-engineer** - Maintain component simplicity

## **Example Complete Component**

```tsx
import { PropsWithChildren, useState } from "react";
import { slugify } from "~utils/slugify";

const DEFAULT_OPTIONS = { sortable: true, filterable: false };
const formatTitle = (title: string) => title.toUpperCase();

type Props = PropsWithChildren<{
  title: string;
  items: string[];
  onSelect?: (item: string) => void;
}>;

const ItemList = ({ children, title, items, onSelect }: Props) => {
  const [selectedItem, setSelectedItem] = useState<string>();

  const handleItemClick = (item: string) => {
    setSelectedItem(item);
    onSelect?.(item);
  };

  return (
    <div className="item-list">
      <h2>{formatTitle(title)}</h2>
      <ul>
        {items.map((item) => (
          <li key={slugify(item)}>
            <button
              onClick={() => handleItemClick(item)}
              className={selectedItem === item ? "selected" : ""}
            >
              {item}
            </button>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
      {children}
    </div>
  );
};

export default ItemList;
```

## **UI Components**

- **Always use shadcn/ui components** - Never create custom UI primitives when shadcn/ui equivalent exists
- **Import from `#ui`** - Use the module alias for all UI component imports, never `#ui`
- **Check existing components first** - Review `src/modules/ui/` before creating custom UI elements
- **Add missing components to `#ui`** using shadcn/ui before creating custom ones

### **Import Paths**

```tsx
// ✅ DO: Use #ui alias
import { Button } from "#ui/button";
import { Input } from "#ui/input";
import {
  Select,
  SelectContent,
  SelectItem,
  SelectTrigger,
  SelectValue,
} from "#ui/select";
import { Dialog, DialogContent, DialogHeader, DialogTitle } from "#ui/dialog";

// ❌ DON'T: Use full module path
import { Button } from "#ui/button";
import { Input } from "#ui/input";
```

### **Available shadcn/ui Components**

Use these existing components from `#ui/`:

- **Form Controls**: `Button`, `Input`, `Textarea`, `Select`, `Checkbox`
- **Layout**: `Card`, `Separator`, `Tabs`
- **Feedback**: `Alert`, `Badge`, `Dialog`
- **Navigation**: `DropdownMenu`

### **Proper Component Usage**

```tsx
// ✅ DO: Use existing shadcn/ui components with proper structure
import { Button } from "#ui/button";
import { Card, CardHeader, CardTitle, CardContent } from "#ui/card";
import {
  Select,
  SelectTrigger,
  SelectContent,
  SelectItem,
  SelectValue,
} from "#ui/select";
import {
  Dialog,
  DialogTrigger,
  DialogContent,
  DialogHeader,
  DialogTitle,
} from "#ui/dialog";

const MyComponent = () => (
  <Card>
    <CardHeader>
      <CardTitle>Example Form</CardTitle>
    </CardHeader>
    <CardContent>
      <div className="space-y-4">
        <Select>
          <SelectTrigger>
            <SelectValue placeholder="Select option..." />
          </SelectTrigger>
          <SelectContent>
            <SelectItem value="option1">Option 1</SelectItem>
            <SelectItem value="option2">Option 2</SelectItem>
          </SelectContent>
        </Select>
        <Dialog>
          <DialogTrigger asChild>
            <Button>Open Dialog</Button>
          </DialogTrigger>
          <DialogContent>
            <DialogHeader>
              <DialogTitle>Dialog Title</DialogTitle>
            </DialogHeader>
            <p>Dialog content...</p>
          </DialogContent>
        </Dialog>
      </div>
    </CardContent>
  </Card>
);

// ❌ DON'T: Create custom UI primitives when shadcn/ui exists
const CustomButton = ({ children }: any) => (
  <button className="custom-btn">{children}</button>
);
const CustomSelect = ({ options }: any) => (
  <select className="custom-select">
    {options.map((opt: any) => (
      <option key={opt.value}>{opt.label}</option>
    ))}
  </select>
);
```

### **Adding New UI Components**

When you need a component not in `#ui/`:

1. **Check shadcn/ui catalog**: https://ui.shadcn.com/docs/components
2. **Add to `src/modules/ui/`** using shadcn/ui CLI or manual setup
3. **Export from `src/modules/ui/index.ts`** for easy imports

```bash
# Add new shadcn/ui component
npx shadcn-ui@latest add [component-name]
```

**Follow these patterns for consistent, maintainable React components.**
